commit 14a2aedb26dc9ab9cbe6473926c9e17b1b96ea18
Author: lora-dataset-studio <noreply@lora-dataset-studio.dev>
Date:   Tue Aug 18 15:10:03 2026 +0200

    fix(captions): a forced dataset pass now keeps its promise to hand-written captions
    
    The caption editor's tooltip and models.py have promised since the origin
    column shipped that a forced 🔄 Re-caption SKIPS 'asserted' rows. The bank pass
    kept that promise from day one; the dataset pass overwrote everything — a
    hand-typed caption included — on every forced batch. Two-surfaces drift, now
    closed on the dataset side:
    
    - a forced BATCH filters caption_origin.unprotected_clause in the same query
      that sizes the run, on both the character/style and concept lanes;
    - naming images (image_ids) is the explicit opt-out: the leak panel re-captions
      a leaking caption no matter who wrote it;
    - a caption typed WHILE an image sits in inference wins over the answer that
      inference returns (the bank's mid-pass guard, ported to every write site);
    - the dual-caption derive pass extends the same promise to hand-written shorts;
    - the Re-caption confirm quotes only what the pass will actually rewrite, and
      the button disables itself when every caption is hand-written instead of
      offering a run that would do nothing.
